      "side": 1,
      "message": "(messages crossed)\n\nhrm... this turned out to be a bit tricky since it means that in the \"usual\" test configuration which defines CONFIG_INTERNAL_STATS PSNR is always calculated it is not possible to not have PSNR calculated which is what the newly added DatarateTestPsnr does.\n\nI locally set that flag to 0 and ran the full test suite (as do the bots?) which suggests that all tests that need PSNR set AOM_CODEC_USE_PSNR? So changing that should be safe and maybe even reduces test time.\n\nBut wrapping it in an `if` does not work as I need it to work since one can no longer use the flag to say \"I do not want PSNR on this frame\" after asking for it once. Which then meant that fiddling with CONFIG_INTERNAL_STATS was no longer required.",
      "parentUuid": "e62f5e1c_fb481346",
      "revId": "5a79200c31b8f9cbe665a014ff0801e722f08d58",
